From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: align the debayer output stride for GPU import

The debayered buffers are handed to userspace as dma-bufs and are routinely
imported straight into the GPU as textures, but their stride is only rounded
up to a multiple of 8 bytes. Mesa requires a 64-byte aligned pitch and refuses
anything else:

  MESA: error: WSI pitch not properly aligned
  could not create EGL image for plane 0 , EGL error 0x3003

which leaves the application with a black viewfinder and no error it can act
on. The debayered width is the input width less the eight border pixels, so
every sensor mode whose width is a multiple of 16 - which is all of them on
the PineTab2's OV5648 - produces a stride exactly 32 bytes short of alignment:
632x480 RGBA gives 2528, and 2528 mod 64 is 32.

Round up to 64 instead. The padding at the end of each line is never read.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN st_a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp st_b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp	2026-09-18 14:12:37.394218180 +0200
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp	2026-09-18 14:12:37.411412834 +0200
@@ -781,8 +781,19 @@
 	if (getOutputConfig(outputFormat, config) != 0)
 		return std::make_tuple(0, 0);
 
-	/* round up to multiple of 8 for 64 bits alignment */
-	unsigned int stride = (size.width * config.bpp / 8 + 7) & ~7;
+	/*
+	 * Round the stride up to a multiple of 64 bytes.
+	 *
+	 * Eight would be enough for the debayering itself, but these buffers
+	 * are handed to userspace as dma-bufs and are routinely imported
+	 * straight into the GPU as textures. Mesa refuses a pitch that is not
+	 * 64-byte aligned - "WSI pitch not properly aligned", and eglCreateImage
+	 * fails with EGL_BAD_ALLOC - and the debayered width is the input width
+	 * less the eight border pixels, so every sensor mode whose width is a
+	 * multiple of 16 lands exactly 32 bytes short of alignment. The padding
+	 * at the end of each line is never read.
+	 */
+	unsigned int stride = (size.width * config.bpp / 8 + 63) & ~63;
 
 	return std::make_tuple(stride, stride * size.height);
 }
